# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets and local
# machine state out of it entirely. Anything listed here cannot end up in an
# image layer even by accident — a COPY that is too broad still cannot reach it.

# Secrets. .env holds a real RPC URL (which is the provider key) and a Mobula
# key. Runtime configuration is supplied by the platform, never baked in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local machine state and build output. node_modules in particular would carry
# macOS-native binaries into a Linux image.
node_modules
dist
dist-server
dist-web
.cache
.ripcord
.ripcord-data

# Version control and CI.
.git
.github
.gitleaks.toml

# Rendered pages. site/ is the GitHub Pages artifact and has no role in the
# webapp container. The committed Mobula sidecars in calibration/live are kept
# in the build context because the report API indexes them at startup.
site

# Editor, OS and log noise.
.DS_Store
*.log
.vscode
.idea

# Documentation and tests are not needed at runtime. The image is a runtime, not
# a development checkout.
docs
test
*.md
!README.md
